erived from multiple, distributed, heterogeneous sources. The role of a general semantic schema, represented as an ontology, is essential to ensure the correctness and consistency in LOD and make it possible to infer implicit knowledge by reasoning. The growth of LOD creates an opportunity for the discovery of ontological knowledge from its raw RDF data itself to enrich relevant knowledge bases. In this work, we aim at discovering schema-level knowledge in the form of axioms encoded in OWL (Ontology Web Language) from RDF data. The approaches to automated generation of the axioms from recorded RDF facts on the Web may be regarded as a case of inductive reasoning and ontology learning. The instances, represented by RDF triples, play the role of specific observations, from which axioms can be extracted by generalization.Based on the insight that discovering new knowledge is

